   =========================================================
   Min-width and max-width
   =========================================================

   🔹 min-width:
     • Sets the minimum width an element can shrink to
     • Element will never become smaller than this value
     • Useful for maintaining readability on small screens

   🔹 max-width:
     • Sets the maximum width an element can grow to
     • Element will never become wider than this value
     • Useful for preventing overly wide content on large screens

   🔹 Common Usage:
     • Responsive layouts
     • Centered content that adapts to different screen sizes
     • Cards, containers, and main content areas

   🔹 Easy Rule to Remember:
     • min-width → stops shrinking
     • max-width → stops growing
